landing-review: landing 11-5a (the feature and effects passes' GL bring-up), level medium, 2026-09-19

Range main...HEAD at db31335..b08d099, main at db31335; a dedicated read-only
reviewer with the mingw toolchain and objdump, 44 tool uses. NO functional
defect. Two LOW findings, both documentation counting errors. Both verified
against the source before acting.

THE ORDERING, re-derived independently and by a stronger route than the brief
gave it: tagpu_vk_owns_present() is s_ownWin != 0 (tagpu_vk.c:732), written
only by InterlockedExchange in tagpu_vk_own_present() (tagpu_vk.c:714), never
cleared; its one call site is render_vk.c:145, above the while loop. Both
gathers are called from tagpu_native_frame (tagpu_native.c:3295-3296), whose
one call site is tagpu_overlay.c:401 inside tagpu_overlay_draw, whose one call
site is render_vk.c:232 inside that loop. render_ogl.c no longer exists and
render_gdi.c calls nothing tagpu_. So the old else-branch was the only one ever
taken and the new unconditional form is exactly it -- exact, not nearly exact.

THE SHADER TRAP: clean. All four VS/FS literals byte-identical to main, checked
by extraction as well as by the build's own spirv gate, which re-extracts
through the preprocessor and compares three SHA-256s per shader.

THE PRAGMA TRAP: clean, and probed in BOTH directions -- a planted static after
the pop warns in both files, one inside the bracket warns in neither, and the
bare files compile with zero warnings. The brackets are at tagpu_feat.c
344/345/402 and tagpu_fx.c 237/238/299, real directives outside comments.

L1 -- gpu-status §2.69 read "lose 22 GL symbols in feat and 28 in fx, PLUS
getgl's three", which asserts 25 and 31. The totals INCLUDE those three: 19 and
25 gl* entry points, undefined symbols 61 -> 39 and 67 -> 39. It matters
because 11-5d's argument for deleting opengl_utils.{c,h} is "no caller is
left", and an audit with `nm -u` against this note would have found three
fewer than stated and concluded they had been re-added. Corrected.

L2 -- "the include residue in the FIVE files that already make no GL call" is
four (render_gdi.c, tagpu_fps.c, tagpu_render3do.c, tagpu_scaffold.c). The
phantom fifth was tagpu_gui_surf.c: my script tested `"opengl_utils.h" in
source` as a SUBSTRING and matched the comment 11-4b left saying the include
had been REMOVED. The call count in the same script was masked; the include
test was not. And the naive fix is also wrong -- `#include "x.h"` is itself a
string literal, so masking the include test finds zero includers. Both notes
now name the files rather than counting them.

The reviewer's own risky-spot checks, all clean: atlas_setup still has its
caller on every path that needs it and nothing else init_gl did was
gather-relevant; the flash light table is still built, stamped, published in
s_pub.lht and cleared by glreset, with tagpu_vk_fx.c:1516-1520 copying the same
bytes; s_state had no second meaning anywhere; no neighbours were swallowed
(checked by symbol table, not grep -- the only defined symbols lost are _getgl,
_mksh, the deleted statics and fx's `said.4` log flag, and _init_gl had already
been inlined so had no symbol); and the include removal is inert, reproduced
with -include rather than a inserted line so that nothing shifts.

Fixes: ad9b605.
